# ── Node / JS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Android / Gradle ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build outputs. These contain the multi-hundred-MB llama.cpp .so set and the
# APK itself; committing them would balloon the repo for no benefit.
android/app/build/
android/build/
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
.gradle/

# Native build trees produced by the NDK for llama.rn / op-sqlite. They are
# regenerated on the next build and are hundreds of MB each.
.cxx/
**/.cxx/
**/build/intermediates/
**/build/generated/

# Hexagon NPU kernels, copied here by llama.rn's `postinstall`
# (install/download-native-artifacts.js) from node_modules/llama.rn/bin/.
# Upstream binaries, ~3.3 MB, regenerated by `npm install` — nothing here is
# ours to redistribute, and committing them would make the diff unreadable.
android/app/src/main/assets/ggml-hexagon/
android/app/src/main/jniLibs/

# Intermediate scrape artifacts behind the curated model catalogue. The
# deliverables are data/models-official.json and data/models-official.md; the
# underscore-prefixed files are the raw material used to produce them.
data/_*.xml
data/_*.csv
data/_*.json
data/_*.ps1

# The uncensored-model catalogue. The app supports a second model line, but the
# data file is excluded alongside its plan doc (see below) so the two stay
# consistent.
data/models-jailbreak.json


# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Release signing material. The DEBUG keystore next to it is intentionally
# NOT ignored: it is the well-known public Android debug key (password
# "android"), identical on every machine, and the build needs it to produce an
# installable APK.
*.jks
*.keystore
!android/app/debug.keystore
keystore.properties
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime configuration the app writes at first launch, which can contain a
# user's API key. Never commit it; the file lives in app-private storage on a
# device, but a copy can end up in a workspace during debugging.
settings.json
**/settings.json

# ── Editors / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json.example
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Misc ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
coverage/
.detox/

# ── Internal notes, deliberately NOT published ───────────────────────────────
# Competitive research: detailed teardowns of other shipping apps (PocketPal,
# Google AI Edge Gallery, SillyTavern, …). All of it is public information, but
# publishing it for free says more about other people's products than about
# this one.
docs/research-*.md

# The uncensored-model sourcing plan. Legitimate engineering work, but it is a
# liability to tie to a public identity, and nothing here is needed to build or
# understand the app.
docs/jailbreak-models-plan.md

# Working notes accumulated while wiring things up (mock-server evaluations,
# integration scratchpad). Kept locally; not part of the project's story.
docs/test-tools-mock-llm.md
docs/integration-notes.md

